MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Eagles greatest-hits collection feels like a natural next choice because I have been choosing familiar melodic rock and collections of well-known songs.",
    "Peter, Paul and Mary connects with the folk harmonies I enjoy in Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie, while Frankie Valli fits my interest in older pop and mid-sixties hits."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The contemporary country albums miss what I want now: familiar older pop, folk, and rock. A melodic sound alone does not make them feel like natural next choices.",
    "25 could appeal to my interest in vocal pop, but I would pass this time because I am more drawn to revisiting older favorites. The second Eagles collection also appeals, but I would only choose one today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits title seems to count for too much on its own; Keith Urban's collection has that format without matching the music I want today.",
    "The country selections suggest that my interest in melodic rock and folk has been stretched into a broader preference for country music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of older hits and classic collections suggest that familiarity and nostalgia matter more to me right now than discovering a newer album.",
    "The connection among Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie matters to me because of their folk sound and vocals, which makes Peter, Paul and Mary especially appealing."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You understood my interest in melodic music and hit collections, but stretched it too far toward contemporary country instead of familiar older pop, folk, and rock."
}
